IMPORT prelude

-- Do Not Call Register Act 2006 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- can I stop the telemarketing calls?
--
-- SEAT: the consumer called by telemarketers, as the relevant account-holder of the number (or the account-holder's
-- nominee) -- "Can I put my number on the Register? How long does it stay there? Was this call to me allowed: is the caller
-- exempt, did I consent? What can I do about it?". Every exported question is that person's. Where the Act hands a judgment
-- to someone else (whether consent "can reasonably be inferred"; what "would be concluded" about a call's purpose; whether
-- the caller took "reasonable precautions"), it is asked as a fact, and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4 (Australian number; consent; registered charity; registered political party; relevant
-- account-holder; voice call); s 5(1), (7) (telemarketing call); s 11(1)-(6) (the prohibition, consent, the 30-day washing
-- defence, mistake, reasonable precautions); s 14 (eligibility); s 15(a) (who may apply); s 17 (duration); ss 24, 25(3)-(6)
-- (civil penalty orders, maximum penalties for s 11(1), on ACMA's application); s 30(1), (4) (compensation for the victim,
-- within 6 years); s 34 (injunctions, on ACMA's application); s 39(1), (2) (nominees); Schedule 1, clauses 2, 3, 4(1) and 6
-- (designated telemarketing calls: government bodies, registered charities, political parties, independent members,
-- candidates, educational institutions); Schedule 2, clauses 2-4 (consent, the 3-month life of express consent, no consent
-- from a published number); Schedule 3, clause 4 (infringement notice amounts for s 11(1)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 16, compilation date 1 September 2021, includes amendments up to Act No. 13, 2021 (register id
-- C2021C00356), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2006A00088.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
-- NOT DEPOSITED: the Do Not Call Register regulations (kinds of call excluded from "telemarketing call" under s 5(7), extra
-- designated calls under Schedule 1 clause 5, kinds of call carved out of each Schedule 1 exemption, circumstances in which
-- consent may or may not be inferred under Schedule 2 clause 5, deemed nominees under s 39(4)); ACMA's s 18 determinations
-- (form and manner of application, removal from the Register); the value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA). Each
-- regulation-made carve-out is an INPUT flag; penalties are in penalty units.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: marketing faxes (ss 5A, 5B, Part 2A, Schedule 1A); s 12 (contracts with call centres -- the caller's duty, not
-- the consumer's question); Schedule 1 clause 4(2) (calls to an employer about an employee's household number) and clause 7;
-- s 11(7) ancillary liability; ss 19-22 (access by telemarketers, fees, the contracted service provider); s 31 (recovery of
-- financial benefit); Schedule 3 machinery other than the amounts; ACMA's formal warnings (s 40) and functions (s 41);
-- complaints to ACMA (Telecommunications Act 1997, Part 26, not this Act). Text messages and email are the Spam Act 2003, not
-- this Act. Research and survey calls are not named anywhere in the Act: such a call is outside s 5 only if it has none of the
-- s 5(1) purposes, or if the regulations exclude it (an input).
--
-- DATES are numbers YYYYMMDD (1 July 2024 is 20240701). "The period of 3 months beginning on" day D is taken to end the day
-- before the same day-number three months later; "6 years after" day D is over from D + 60000. This is the encoder's
-- convention, not the Act's (a day-number that does not exist in the later month is not handled).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Do Not Call Register Act 2006 -- from the seat of the consumer called by telemarketers`

-- The day three months after day D (YYYYMMDD), rolling the year where the month passes December.
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`three months after` MEANS
    IF (`the day` MODULO 10000) AT LEAST 1000
    THEN `the day` PLUS 10000 MINUS 900
    ELSE `the day` PLUS 300

§§ `ss 14, 15, 17, 39 -- can I register my number, and for how long`

-- s 4: "Australian number" -- a number in the telecommunications numbering plan for carriage services to the public in
-- Australia (asked as a fact). "relevant account-holder ... (a) if an individual or organisation is solely responsible for
-- the relevant account--the individual or organisation; or (b) if 2 or more ... are jointly responsible ... any of those".
-- s 14: "An Australian number is eligible to be entered on the Do Not Call Register if: (a) it is used or maintained
-- primarily for private or domestic purposes; or (b) it is used or maintained exclusively for transmitting and/or receiving
-- faxes; or (c) it is used or maintained exclusively for use by a government body; or (d) it is an emergency service
-- number."
-- s 15: an application "may be made by: (i) the relevant account-holder; or (ii) a nominee of the relevant account-holder".
-- s 39(1), (2): a nominee is an individual the account-holder "has nominated" where "the nomination has not been
-- withdrawn"; a nomination "must be in writing".
-- s 17(1): registration "(a) takes effect when it is entered on the Do Not Call Register; and (b) unless sooner removed from
-- the Do Not Call Register in accordance with a determination under subsection 18(1), remains in force indefinitely."
-- (3): a removed number may be re-registered.
DECLARE `Phone number` HAS
    `is an Australian number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used or maintained primarily for private or domestic purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used or maintained exclusively for faxes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used or maintained exclusively by a government body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an emergency service number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `day entered on the Register` IS A NUMBER
    `day removed from the Register under an ACMA determination` IS A NUMBER

@export Is my phone number eligible to go on the Do Not Call Register (s 14)?
GIVEN `my number` IS A `Phone number` @desc Your phone number and what it is used for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my number eligible for the Register` IF
        `my number`'s `is an Australian number`
    AND (    `my number`'s `used or maintained primarily for private or domestic purposes`
         OR  `my number`'s `used or maintained exclusively for faxes`
         OR  `my number`'s `used or maintained exclusively by a government body`
         OR  `my number`'s `is an emergency service number`)

@export May I apply to put this number on the Do Not Call Register (ss 15, 39)?
GIVEN `I am responsible for the account, alone or jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the account-holder, or one of the joint account-holders, for the number
      `the account-holder has nominated me in writing and not withdrawn it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account-holder nominated you in writing for this number, and the nomination still stands
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to register the number` IF
        `I am responsible for the account, alone or jointly`
    OR  `the account-holder has nominated me in writing and not withdrawn it`

@export Is my number on the Do Not Call Register on a given day (s 17: from entry, indefinitely unless removed)?
GIVEN `my number` IS A `Phone number` @desc Your phone number, with the day it was entered on the Register (0 if never) and the day it was removed (0 if never)
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day in question, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my number registered on` IF
        `my number`'s `day entered on the Register` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `my number`'s `day entered on the Register` AT MOST `the day`
    AND (    `my number`'s `day removed from the Register under an ACMA determination` EQUALS 0
         OR  `the day` LESS THAN `my number`'s `day removed from the Register under an ACMA determination`
         OR  `my number`'s `day removed from the Register under an ACMA determination` LESS THAN `my number`'s `day entered on the Register`)

§§ `s 5 -- is it a telemarketing call`

-- s 5(1): "a telemarketing call is a voice call to an Australian number, where, having regard to: (a) the content of the
-- call; and (b) the presentational aspects of the call; and (c) the content that can be obtained using the numbers, URLs or
-- contact information (if any) mentioned in the call; and (d) [the content obtainable by calling the calling number]; it
-- would be concluded that the purpose, or one of the purposes, of the call is: (e) to offer to supply goods or services; ...
-- (h) to offer to supply land or an interest in land; ... (k) to offer to provide a business opportunity or investment
-- opportunity; ... (n) to solicit donations; or (o) a purpose specified in the regulations."
-- s 4: "voice call" includes "a call that involves a recorded or synthetic voice". A text message is not a voice call.
-- s 5(2), (3): it is immaterial whether the goods or opportunity exist or are lawful. s 5(7): "The regulations may provide
-- that a specified kind of voice call is not a telemarketing call" -- an INPUT.
DECLARE `Kind of caller` IS ONE OF
    `a government body`
    `a registered charity`
    `a registered political party`
    `a member of parliament or a local council not affiliated with a registered party`
    `a candidate in an election`
    `an educational institution`
    `any other business or person`

DECLARE `Call` HAS
    `to my number` IS A `Phone number`
    `day of the call` IS A NUMBER
    `is a voice call, live, recorded or synthetic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purpose is to offer or promote goods, services, land or a business or investment opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purpose is to solicit donations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purpose is a further purpose specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of a kind the regulations say is not a telemarketing call` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by` IS A `Kind of caller`
    `relates to goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the authorising body is the supplier or prospective supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purpose is fund-raising for electoral or political purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I or a member of my household is or was enrolled at the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of a kind the regulations carve out of its Schedule 1 exemption` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is this call a telemarketing call under the Do Not Call Register Act (s 5)?
GIVEN `the call` IS A `Call` @desc The call you received: what it was, who authorised it, and what it was for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a telemarketing call` IF
        `the call`'s `is a voice call, live, recorded or synthetic`
    AND `the call`'s `to my number`'s `is an Australian number`
    AND (    `the call`'s `a purpose is to offer or promote goods, services, land or a business or investment opportunity`
         OR  `the call`'s `a purpose is to solicit donations`
         OR  `the call`'s `a purpose is a further purpose specified in the regulations`)
    AND (NOT `the call`'s `is of a kind the regulations say is not a telemarketing call`)

-- The bridge to the Privacy Act baseline (APP 7.8): "This principle does not apply to the extent that any of the following
-- apply: (a) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006". The Privacy Act baseline asks it as a fact; this is that fact for a call.
@export Does the Do Not Call Register Act reach this call, so that APP 7 of the Privacy Act gives way to it (APP 7.8)?
GIVEN `the call` IS A `Call` @desc The call you received
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this Act reach the call` IF `Is it a telemarketing call` `the call`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- which callers are exempt`

-- Sch 1 cl 2: "a telemarketing call is a designated telemarketing call if: (a) the making of the call is authorised by ...
-- (i) a government body; (ii) a registered charity; and (b) if the call relates to goods or services--the body is the
-- supplier, or prospective supplier, of the goods or services; and (c) the call is not of a kind specified in the
-- regulations."
-- cl 3(1)-(3): a call authorised by a registered political party, an unaffiliated member of a parliament or local governing
-- body, or a candidate, where "it would be concluded that the purpose, or one of the purposes, of the call is: (iii) to
-- conduct fund-raising for electoral purposes; or (iv) to conduct fund-raising for political purposes", with the same
-- supplier and regulations conditions.
-- cl 4(1): a call authorised by an educational institution, to a number "used or maintained primarily for the private or
-- domestic purposes of the relevant account-holder and/or members of the relevant account-holder's household", where the
-- account-holder or "a member or former member of the relevant account-holder's household is, or has been, enrolled as a
-- student in that institution", with the same supplier and regulations conditions.
-- cl 6: an individual authorising on behalf of an organisation is taken not to authorise -- the organisation does; a caller
-- not authorised by anyone else authorises its own call. "Authorised by" is asked as a fact read with cl 6.
-- No other caller is exempt in the Act. Market and social research, and businesses with an existing relationship, are not
-- named; an existing relationship counts only through inferred consent (Schedule 2 cl 2(b)).
GIVEN `the call` IS A `Call`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier and regulations conditions are met` IF
        ((NOT `the call`'s `relates to goods or services`) OR `the call`'s `the authorising body is the supplier or prospective supplier`)
    AND (NOT `the call`'s `is of a kind the regulations carve out of its Schedule 1 exemption`)

@export Is this call exempt as a designated telemarketing call (Schedule 1: government, charities, political fund-raising, my school or university)?
GIVEN `the call` IS A `Call` @desc The call you received: who authorised it and what it was for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the caller exempt` IF
        `the supplier and regulations conditions are met` `the call`
    AND (CONSIDER `the call`'s `authorised by`
         WHEN `a government body` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a registered charity` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a registered political party` THEN `the call`'s `a purpose is fund-raising for electoral or political purposes`
         WHEN `a member of parliament or a local council not affiliated with a registered party` THEN `the call`'s `a purpose is fund-raising for electoral or political purposes`
         WHEN `a candidate in an election` THEN `the call`'s `a purpose is fund-raising for electoral or political purposes`
         WHEN `an educational institution` THEN
                  `the call`'s `to my number`'s `used or maintained primarily for private or domestic purposes`
              AND `the call`'s `I or a member of my household is or was enrolled at the institution`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `Schedule 2 -- did I consent`

-- Sch 2 cl 2: "consent means: (a) express consent; or (b) consent that can reasonably be inferred from: (i) the conduct; and
-- (ii) the business and other relationships; of the individual or organisation concerned."
-- cl 3: if express consent "is not expressed to be for a specified period or for an indefinite period; the consent is taken
-- to have been withdrawn at the end of the period of 3 months beginning on the day on which the consent was given."
-- cl 4: consent "may not be inferred from the mere fact that the number has been published."
-- s 11(2): the consent that counts is that of "(a) the relevant account-holder; or (b) a nominee of the relevant
-- account-holder". Whether consent "can reasonably be inferred" is a judgment: an INPUT, read subject to cl 4.
DECLARE `How long my express consent was to last` IS ONE OF
    `no period was stated`
    `until a stated day`
    `indefinitely`

DECLARE `My consent` HAS
    `I or my nominee gave express consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `day the express consent was given` IS A NUMBER
    `stated length` IS A `How long my express consent was to last`
    `the stated last day` IS A NUMBER
    `I or my nominee withdrew it before the call` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent can reasonably be inferred from my conduct and business and other relationships` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only ground for inferring it is that my number was published` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Was my express consent to telemarketing calls still in force on the day of the call (Schedule 2 cl 3: 3 months if no period stated)?
GIVEN `my consent` IS A `My consent` @desc The consent you gave, when, and for how long
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the call, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my express consent in force on` IF
        `my consent`'s `I or my nominee gave express consent`
    AND (NOT `my consent`'s `I or my nominee withdrew it before the call`)
    AND `my consent`'s `day the express consent was given` AT MOST `the day`
    AND (CONSIDER `my consent`'s `stated length`
         WHEN `indefinitely` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `until a stated day` THEN `the day` AT MOST `my consent`'s `the stated last day`
         WHEN `no period was stated` THEN `the day` LESS THAN `three months after` (`my consent`'s `day the express consent was given`))

@export Did I consent to the call, expressly or by inference from my conduct and relationships (Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my consent` IS A `My consent` @desc The consent you gave, and your dealings with the caller
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the call, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I consent to the call` IF
        `Was my express consent in force on` `my consent` `the day`
    OR  (    `my consent`'s `consent can reasonably be inferred from my conduct and business and other relationships`
         AND (NOT `my consent`'s `the only ground for inferring it is that my number was published`))

§§ `s 11 -- was the call to me allowed`

-- s 11(1): "A person must not make, or cause to be made, a telemarketing call to an Australian number if: (a) the number is
-- registered on the Do Not Call Register; and (b) the call is not a designated telemarketing call."
-- (2): it does not apply if the account-holder or nominee "consented to the making of the call".
-- (3): nor if the number was on a list the caller submitted to the Register and, "during the 30-day period ending at the end
-- of the day on which the call was made", the caller was told it was not registered.
-- (4): nor if the call was made "by mistake" (s 4: "reasonable mistake of fact"). (5): nor if the caller "took reasonable
-- precautions, and exercised due diligence, to avoid the contravention". (6): the caller "bears an evidential burden".
-- (9): a business that contracts with a call centre "is taken to have caused" the calls the call centre makes.
-- The defences are the caller's to raise, and a court's to accept: an INPUT.
DECLARE `Call answer` IS ONE OF
    `allowed: it is not a telemarketing call under this Act`
    `allowed: my number was not on the Register on the day of the call`
    `allowed: the caller is exempt under Schedule 1`
    `allowed: I or my nominee consented`
    `forbidden by s 11(1), but the caller has a defence under s 11(3), (4) or (5)`
    `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it`

@export Was this telemarketing call to my number allowed (s 11)?
GIVEN `the call` IS A `Call` @desc The call you received
      `my consent` IS A `My consent` @desc Any consent you gave, and your dealings with the caller
      `the caller has a defence accepted under s 11(3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caller shows it checked the Register within 30 days and was told the number was not on it, made a reasonable mistake of fact, or took reasonable precautions and due diligence
GIVETH A `Call answer`
DECIDE `Was the call allowed` IS
    IF NOT `Is it a telemarketing call` `the call`
    THEN `allowed: it is not a telemarketing call under this Act`
    ELSE IF NOT `Is my number registered on` (`the call`'s `to my number`) (`the call`'s `day of the call`)
         THEN `allowed: my number was not on the Register on the day of the call`
         ELSE IF `Is the caller exempt` `the call`
              THEN `allowed: the caller is exempt under Schedule 1`
              ELSE IF `Did I consent to the call` `my consent` (`the call`'s `day of the call`)
                   THEN `allowed: I or my nominee consented`
                   ELSE IF `the caller has a defence accepted under s 11(3), (4) or (5)`
                        THEN `forbidden by s 11(1), but the caller has a defence under s 11(3), (4) or (5)`
                        ELSE `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it`

§§ `ss 24, 30, 34 -- what can I do about it`

-- s 24(1): a civil penalty order is made "on the application of the ACMA". s 34(1), (2): an injunction is granted "on the
-- application of the ACMA". Neither section gives the person called an application of their own.
-- s 30(1): if, "in one or more proceedings under section 24", the court "finds that a person (the perpetrator) has
-- contravened one or more civil penalty provisions" and "is satisfied that another person (the victim) has suffered loss or
-- damage", it "may, on the application of the ACMA or the victim", order compensation. (2): the court may have regard to
-- the victim's expenses of "dealing with the calls", the effect on the victim's business or other activities, reputation
-- and lost opportunities. (3): with or without a civil penalty order. (4): "within 6 years after the contravention".
-- Complaints to the ACMA are made under the Telecommunications Act 1997 (s 3 note), not this Act.
DECLARE `Remedy answer` IS ONE OF
    `nothing under this Act: the call was not forbidden`
    `nothing under this Act: the caller made out a defence`
    `I have no application of my own: only the ACMA may seek a civil penalty or an injunction (ss 24, 34)`
    `I may apply to the court for compensation for my loss or damage (s 30)`
    `too late: more than 6 years have passed since the call (s 30(4))`

@export What can I do under this Act about a telemarketing call made to me (ss 24, 30, 34)?
GIVEN `the answer about the call` IS A `Call answer` @desc Whether the call was allowed under s 11
      `the court has found the contravention in ACMA's civil penalty proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, in proceedings the ACMA brought under s 24, has found that the caller contravened the Act
      `I suffered loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered loss or damage from the calls, such as costs or lost business
      `day of the call` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the call, as YYYYMMDD
      `today` IS A NUMBER @desc Today, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Remedy answer`
DECIDE `What can I do about the call` IS
    IF `the answer about the call` EQUALS `forbidden by s 11(1), but the caller has a defence under s 11(3), (4) or (5)`
    THEN `nothing under this Act: the caller made out a defence`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the answer about the call` EQUALS `forbidden by s 11(1): the caller contravened it`)
         THEN `nothing under this Act: the call was not forbidden`
         ELSE IF `today` AT LEAST (`day of the call` PLUS 60000)
              THEN `too late: more than 6 years have passed since the call (s 30(4))`
              ELSE IF `the court has found the contravention in ACMA's civil penalty proceedings` AND `I suffered loss or damage`
                   THEN `I may apply to the court for compensation for my loss or damage (s 30)`
                   ELSE `I have no application of my own: only the ACMA may seek a civil penalty or an injunction (ss 24, 34)`

§§ `s 25, Schedule 3 cl 4 -- what the caller can be made to pay`

-- s 25(3)(a)(i): a body corporate with no prior record, for a contravention of s 11(1), "100 penalty units"; (4)(a)(i): a
-- person other than a body corporate, "20 penalty units"; (5)(a)(i), (6)(a)(i): with a prior record, 500 and 100.
-- (3)(b), (4)(b), (5)(b), (6)(b): for 2 or more contraventions on one day, totals of 2,000, 400, 10,000 and 2,000.
-- Sch 3 cl 4(1) items 1-3: an infringement notice to a body corporate for s 11(1) is 20 penalty units for one alleged
-- contravention, "20 by the number" for more than 1 but fewer than 50, and 1,000 for 50 or more; cl 4(2): to any other
-- person, 4, 4 by the number, and 200. The dollar value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914, not this Act.
@export What is the most a court can order the caller to pay, in penalty units, for one call to a registered number (s 25)?
GIVEN `the caller is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caller is a company or other body corporate
      `the caller has a prior civil penalty order under s 11(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already made a civil penalty order against the caller for s 11(1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the caller can be ordered to pay for one call` IS
    IF `the caller is a body corporate`
    THEN IF `the caller has a prior civil penalty order under s 11(1)` THEN 500 ELSE 100
    ELSE IF `the caller has a prior civil penalty order under s 11(1)` THEN 100 ELSE 20

@export How many penalty units is an infringement notice to the caller for calls to registered numbers (Schedule 3 cl 4)?
GIVEN `the caller is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caller is a company or other body corporate
      `the number of calls in the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many alleged contraventions of s 11(1) the notice covers
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many penalty units is the infringement notice` IS
    IF `the caller is a body corporate`
    THEN IF `the number of calls in the notice` AT LEAST 50 THEN 1000 ELSE 20 TIMES `the number of calls in the notice`
    ELSE IF `the number of calls in the notice` AT LEAST 50 THEN 200 ELSE 4 TIMES `the number of calls in the notice`
